      simpleExplanation: "Normally, Islamic law requires that whatever you sell must already exist and belong to you. Salam and Istisna'a are two special exceptions to that rule - they let you sell something that doesn't exist yet, as long as you follow extra conditions designed to remove the uncertainty (Gharar) that would otherwise make such a sale risky and unfair.",
